[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hey y'all <span aria-label=\"man raising hand\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f64b-200d-2642\" role=\"img\" title=\"man raising hand\">:man_raising_hand:</span></p>\n<p>I'm messing around with a very basic simplifier similar to what you'd find in a computer algebra library:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/dharmatech/symbolism.lean\">https://github.com/dharmatech/symbolism.lean</a></p>\n<p>This is mostly for me to explore the Lean language a bit.</p>\n<p>I'm not yet familiar with the Lean idioms so the code is likely to be a bit unusual in places.</p>\n<p>I'm really impressed with Lean's expressiveness on a project like this.<br>\nThe code is a rough port from a C# library and the ideas are very concisely expressed in Lean.</p>\n<p>If there are already existing computer algebra libraries like this (i.e. not for theorem proving but for symbolic expression manipulation) feel free to mention them below.</p>\n<p>The source for the simplifier is here:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/dharmatech/symbolism.lean/blob/master/Symbolism/Basic.lean\">https://github.com/dharmatech/symbolism.lean/blob/master/Symbolism/Basic.lean</a></p>\n<p>The unit tests show some examples of the simplifications:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/dharmatech/symbolism.lean/blob/master/SymbolismTests.lean\">https://github.com/dharmatech/symbolism.lean/blob/master/SymbolismTests.lean</a></p>",
        "id": 585004569,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo Cavazos",
        "timestamp": 1775967341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have any plans to continue? For example, it would be nice if</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">simplify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>worked (or similar).</p>",
        "id": 585182327,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Dvořák",
        "timestamp": 1776085019
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"417654\">Martin Dvořák</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Computer.20algebra.20simplifier/near/585182327\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Do you have any plans to continue? For example, it would be nice if</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">simplify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>worked (or similar).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Hey Martin <span aria-label=\"man raising hand\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f64b-200d-2642\" role=\"img\" title=\"man raising hand\">:man_raising_hand:</span></p>\n<p>Good question.</p>\n<p>In <code>symbolism.lean</code>, <code>Expr.simplify</code> does what some call \"automatic simplification\".<br>\nThis is the basic simplification you'd get when you enter an expression at the prompt of a computer algebra system like Mathematica, Maple, Sympy, etc.</p>\n<p>To get something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>in Sympy, you'd need to call <code>expand</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">python</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Python</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">3.14</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tags</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">v3</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">14</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ebf955d</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Oct</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2025</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">15</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">03</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MSC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1944</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AMD64</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">win32</span>\n<span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"help\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"copyright\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"credits\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"license\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">more</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">information</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sympy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"n\">x'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"n\">y'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expand</span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In Mathematica, you'd use <code>Expand</code>:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"676x302\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/Zxr74icVnhw7bSDgr4enu81p/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/Zxr74icVnhw7bSDgr4enu81p/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>In <code>Symbolism.cs</code>, the C# library that <code>symbolism.lean</code> is based on, we'd use <code>AlgebraicExpand</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"x\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"y\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result_0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result_0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AlgebraicExpand</span><span class=\"o\">()</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WriteLine</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result_0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">Console</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WriteLine</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result_1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Output of that C# program:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So for <code>symbolism.lean</code>, one option would be to implement something like <code>AlgebraicExpand</code>.<br>\nThe C# source for that is here:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/dharmatech/Symbolism/blob/master/Symbolism/AlgebraicExpand.cs\">https://github.com/dharmatech/Symbolism/blob/master/Symbolism/AlgebraicExpand.cs</a></p>\n<p>Right now in <code>symbolism.lean</code>, I've kept things limited to just a really minimal automatic-simplification algorithm to get a feel for Lean. I haven't implemented any of the utility functions. More examples of these in the C# version are here:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/dharmatech/Symbolism/tree/master/Symbolism\">https://github.com/dharmatech/Symbolism/tree/master/Symbolism</a></p>\n<p>So it should be doable! I just haven't explored that on the Lean side yet.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your question!</p>",
        "id": 585264636,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo Cavazos",
        "timestamp": 1776107554
    }
]